      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Sertraline 400 mg daily is twice the FDA-labeled maximum for adults, which is 200 mg/day. Doses above that raise the risk of serotonin syndrome, seizures, QT prolongation, and GI and CNS adverse effects. They have no proven added benefit. Your patient's normal kidney and liver function and lack of allergies don't change that limit.\n\nCould you check a few things?\n- **Typo or miscalculation:** Did you mean 40 mg or 100 mg? Or 200 mg, the maximum?\n- **Usual dosing:** Adults typically start at 25\u201350 mg daily and titrate by 25\u201350 mg at intervals of at least one week. The usual range is 50\u2013200 mg daily.\n- **Deliberate high dose:** If your attending or psychiatry wants a dose above the labeled maximum, I'd confirm that with them and with pharmacy first. I'd also document the rationale in the order note.\n\nTell me the corrected dose, or confirm that the attending or pharmacy approved 400 mg, and I'll enter it right away."
      }
